*.log

# Node
# NO trailing slash. `node_modules/` matches DIRECTORIES ONLY, so a symlink
# named node_modules — which is what a shared-install worktree has — sailed
# straight past it and got committed by `git add -A` (2026-08-29). That
# symlink pointed outside the repo, so on the Pages runner it dangled and
# `tar --dereference` failed the deploy: plursky.com sat on a stale build
# while main moved two versions ahead.
node_modules
dist/

